       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in hyperkalemia:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " a helpful adjunct: albuterol 10 to 20 mg inhaled over 10 min can ↓K by 0.5 to 1.5 mEq/L; peak effect at 90 min; CI in unstable angina or acute MI."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " hypersensitivity to any ingredient. Caution in CVD (coronary insuff, arrhythmias, HTN); ECG chgs (T-wave flattening, QTc prolongation, ST depression) are reported."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "BBs block the effect and can cause severe bronchospasm in asthma (cardioselective only, w caution, if ⍉alt). Loop/thiazide diuretics: hypokalemia and ECG chgs can worsen. Digoxin levels may fall; consider monitoring. MAOIs/TCAs (or w.in 2 wks of stopping): extreme caution, vasc effects potentiated."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
